<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Cameroon govt announces payments as teachers strike continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa795b72ae90f9a0b41bbb246d235c3b5415fc31eff35f901a7239296485b683</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-cameroon-govt-announces-payments-as-teachers-strike-continues" /><summary type="html">In Cameroon, the start of the academic year for Universities, scheduled for October 5, may not take place. This is as a result of an indefinite strike launched by SYNES, the National Union of Higher Education Teachers. Teachers are demanding the payment of 16 billion CFA francs in academic bonuses, equivalent to nearly 24 million euros.</summary></entry><entry><title>A blessing or a curse? New Caledonia's dwindling nickel industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d55006b9f19f21e93da4456adc9ba856b2a81f6404b86a9ae185e280e9a8dc</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:39:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry" /><summary type="html">This Thursday October 1, the French government is holding a summit aimed at attracting investors and revitalising wealth creation in France's overseas territories. Among the assets Paris wants to highlight is New Caledonian nickel. But the industry has been severely weakened by the political deadlock and tensions that have rocked the archipelago in recent years.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Sheer devastation: '80 percent of Gazan infrastructure has been destroyed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01981196183fafb08cf61fdfeb6ffa1783b56a1e8a626c15149759748010ad0d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed" /><summary type="html">New images posted this week by Google Maps show the utter destruction in Gaza. It's been estimated that 61 tonnes of rubble need to be cleared – that's 20 times the amount of rubble generated in all wars across the world over the last 18 years.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>From Billie Eilish to Cardi B: Hassan Hajjaj on the stars who stepped into his colourful world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e845ec3dba84abb92125bc74aea806be713ba2ac134d7a5255fc9ae86af49058</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:06:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261001-from-billie-eilish-to-cardi-b-hassan-hajjaj-on-the-stars-who-stepped-into-his-colourful-world" /><summary type="html">Moroccan-British artist and photographer Hassan Hajjaj has photographed some of the biggest names in music and pop culture – from Madonna, Billie Eilish and Alicia Keys to Cardi B and Lee "Scratch" Perry. Now, 40 of his vibrant "Rock Stars" are on show at Paris's Philharmonie. Hajjaj tells us how he creates his instantly recognisable portraits, blends Moroccan heritage with London street culture – and what happens when a global superstar steps in front of his camera.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Behind the scenes of Céline Dion's high-tech gig - Tech 24</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4103c450c561fbbbed3b21d62c41ef4db5e96baf03fc089929a1dfc2543e8d2</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:03:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-behind-the-scenes-of-c%C3%A9line-dion-s-high-tech-gig-tech-24" /><summary type="html">🎤 #CélineDion is making her great comeback with a 16-day residency in #France after years of illness. To keep her stage quiet and her voice crisp, her team is using both AI and high-tech sound systems.
 
#FRANCE24's Peter O'Brien went behind the scenes at the invitation of French audio company L-Acoustics ☝️</summary></entry><entry><title>UK, France end 'on in, one out' Channel migrant exchange deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228fdc168cefd49d394bc3667d223882abc55c5c97a6dc9cefa6b0613edc9560</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:44:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-uk-france-end-on-in-one-out-channel-migrant-exchange-deal" /><summary type="html">A year-old deal between France and Britain to return migrants crossing the Channel illegally on small boats has come to an end, the UK interior ministry said Wednesday. The deal was agreed under former UK prime minister Keir Starmer last year in a bid to help a post-Brexit reset by easing what had become a major source of tension between the neighbours.</summary></entry><entry><title>France demands belt-tightening in 2027 budget as investors sour on its debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8196ff28da9d252b7da896cdfa6e36302b9c2998ffbf711b6ff1a6eb0a01b9c3</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:42:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-demands-belt-tightening-in-2027-budget-as-investors-sour-on-its-debt" /><summary type="html">France presented its ​2027 budget bill on Thursday, seeking to enact unpopular belt-tightening measures that can lower its deficit and appease increasingly twitchy bond investors ahead of next year's presidential election. The legislation faces a tough ride in a deeply divided parliament, as political clans position themselves for one of the country's most consequential elections in modern times.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s 2027 budget plan puts pressure on local services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb370f916a17abcc7646ce77b7986ac5340c8a08cf1f5f921299bf4b65d4c6e6</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:42:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-s-2027-budget-plan-puts-pressure-on-local-services" /><summary type="html">France presented its ​2027 budget bill on Thursday, seeking to enact unpopular belt-tightening measures. And local governments are bracing for painful cuts. The national government provides most of the financing for local and municipal budgets – and it's now seeking 5.4 billion euros in savings there. Across the country, mayors are scrambling to figure out how to cut back, while still providing essential services.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pink October: Raising awareness about breast cancer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4c9049e40f068808fb1077d121324e2a97479b9e442c4939a9735eb585abe79</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:40:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-pink-october-raising-awareness-about-breast-cancer" /><summary type="html">Breast cancer is the leading cause of cancer-related deaths among women and more than 61,000 cases are diagnosed in France each year. At Paris's Curie Institute, researchers are trying to develop new ways to identify and treat different types of cancers. One trial involves developing so-called “tumors on a chip”: miniature models which are capable of recreating the characteristics of a tumor in vitro outside of their normal biological context.</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know about the terrifying FlyDubai flight bound for Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:157b40d9e37ccddcf609c8d4bc3db4d6cffa868c6897c16e048db0f61d6d8f9f</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:38:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-what-to-know-about-the-terrifying-flydubai-flight-bound-for-israel" /><summary type="html">A copilot stabbed a captain in an apparent attempt to crash a jetliner as it was flying 174 people to Israel on Wednesday. But passengers burst into the cockpit and wrestled with the attacker even as the plane descended sharply, witnesses and Israel’s government said. The plane made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia. The shaken passengers from the FlyDubai flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv landed Wednesday evening in Israel on another flight, as onlookers cheered.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gender-based violence: French proposed bill aims to strengthen protections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44c521371103b932cdb5e7f2d6960c9f0730a3c0498f203534ab418f509205f6</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:37:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-gender-based-violence-french-proposed-bill-aims-to-strengthen-protections" /><summary type="html">French lawmakers are set to debate a bill against gender-based and sexual violence. It aims to strengthen the entire process – from reporting crimes and investigation to protection and compensation for victims. The bill also targets online sexual abuse, including non-consensual content and AI-generated deepfakes. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hundreds held, dozens wounded as French school protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c8fe7888a59af2a554963712df2fb5d7a3f907c5d2fa1e6395436e3f71cd81a</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-hundreds-held-dozens-wounded-as-french-school-protests-escalate" /><summary type="html">French security forces on Wednesday detained over 600 people while dozens of police and gendarmes were wounded as protests that have seen blockades of high schools and violent clashes escalated, the interior minister said. Since last week, students have staged protests outside schools over grievances ranging from timetables, class sizes and a shortage of teachers to overheated classrooms during this year's heatwaves. FRANCE 24's Caroline Baum reports from Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>The hunting lobby: Behind France's rural power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7d607bb1eeaf3e7435abb5d57986ec264cfff1bd7e2eba80628566c91ea04ae</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:24:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261001-the-hunting-lobby-behind-france-s-rural-power" /><summary type="html">After football and fishing, France's third-favourite pastime is hunting. The ancestral activity is popular but also divisive, with passions running high between those who defend hunting traditions and a growing number of animal rights activists. Though it's become statistically safer, a majority of French people say they don’t feel secure walking in nature during hunting season. So what steps has the government taken to regulate hunting? And why is the hunting lobby so strong and influential? We take a closer look in this edition of French Connections.</summary><category term="French connections" /></entry><entry><title>US continues to be 'a very significant partner', UN peacekeeping chief says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fbd3228de34cf57c39f99f424dccc68250d8ab495177e8c3b8c779ff7e5edc6</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:14:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN peacekeeping chief Jean-Pierre Lacroix said the US continues to be "a very significant partner", despite owing $3 billion to peacekeeping. With the UN forced to cut about 25 percent of its capacity, Lacroix defended missions that cost just 0.2 percent of global military spending: "Peacekeeping is a good deal really."</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee death row inmate Christa Pike survives two lethal injections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9e749bef94c0f28da434f5df5a9e030ca7900c402534b531568de311b3e70a2</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:41:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-tennessee-death-row-inmate-christa-pike-survives-two-lethal-injections" /><summary type="html">A Tennessee woman convicted of a murder three decades ago survived two lethal injection doses on Wednesday, marking the state's second failed execution this year. Christa Pike, 50, had been set to become the first woman to be executed in the southern US state in 200 years. The botched execution prompted the state’s governor to halt the one remaining execution for the rest of the year and launch a “comprehensive review”.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why are French students blocking their school entrances?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4736b558b1126afe1da9182cded9528e1a57b624a83d95f8ef20245d79508d0e</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-why-are-french-students-blocking-their-school-entrances" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 🎒 🪧 High schoolers across #France continued to blockade their #schools on Thursday, trying to form a "blocus" at the entrances of their schools in #protest.
 
French Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez said that 625 people, mostly students, had been detained during blockade attempts on Wednesday, noting "an expansion of the movement".
 
But what are they asking for? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's Netanyahu says co-pilot tried to crash Tel Aviv-bound plane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:355a2a9bfcea6a70bb76f38298a79124fbf36ac554031ce55c527d75901d5010</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:00:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261001-israel-s-netanyahu-says-co-pilot-tried-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-plane" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 1: A FlyDubai flight was diverted to Saudi Arabia after the pilot was stabbed by his co-pilot in what the Israeli media are calling a terror attack. The co-pilot was detained by off-duty pilots on board and passengers before making a safe landing in Saudi Arabia. Also in the news, Cornell University's college campus culture is back under scrutiny after a shocking sexual assault claim. Plus, a man learns that Singapore does not take AI slop lightly.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil elections: Can Lula’s anti-poverty record win over voters?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da99a98dbf9f42c1ff58232fba0f31067813378112c4f9327c5f67a2c6360037</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:51:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-brazil-elections-can-lula-s-anti-poverty-record-win-over-voters" /><summary type="html">In Brazil, incumbent President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva is seeking a fourth and final term in the presidential election on October 4. In 2022, he made the fight against hunger and poverty a key campaign promise. Between 2023 and 2024, nearly nine million people were lifted out of poverty thanks to the government’s social and economic programs. The decline was particularly sharp in Brazil’s Northeast. A traditional stronghold for Lula, will the progress made in reducing poverty translate into stronger support for the current president? FRANCE 24's team on the ground reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Burnham reopens Brexit debate: EU says UK must chart Its own path on future relations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:416e1223f197eb83e092482845a02cc82550714a745c242bf21aba3cb7c5ce93</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:46:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-burnham-reopens-brexit-debate-eu-says-uk-must-chart-its-own-path-on-future-relations" /><summary type="html">The EU said Wednesday it was up to London to chart a way forward for Britain's relations with the bloc, after Prime Minister Andy Burnham put the idea of rejoining on the table. Burnham reopened the divisive Brexit debate Wednesday by saying his centre-left Labour government could go "all the way" and propose membership of the bloc, once it has weighed the "pros and cons" of different possible relationships with Europe. For the European perspective, FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tennessee death row inmate Christa Pike survives execution attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b83ed7b55ef61de3fe1963d041738c1dcd4db0cc0b7ac60f33690edd7b27a6af</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:44:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-tennessee-death-row-inmate-christa-pike-survives-execution-attempt" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike, convicted of murdering a schoolmate three decades ago, survived Tennessee's effort to execute her by means of lethal injection late on Wednesday, prison officials said, foiling the state's first attempt to put a woman to death in two centuries. Pike's condition following the ordeal was not immediately known, and it was not clear what legal avenues her lawyers or the state might pursue ​next after she was ‌taken for medical treatment from the Riverbend Maximum Security Institution in Nashville.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hegseth 'state of the force' speech: US to cut number of generals, admirals by 20%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e3e916e0f8dc4c75dd9afb0eaf88db13bcf3c17d764d3db4de39668d2b13acd</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:42:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-hegseth-state-of-the-force-speech-us-to-cut-number-of-generals-admirals-by-20" /><summary type="html">Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth announced Wednesday that the United States has slashed the number of its generals and admirals by 20 percent, in a move he said is aimed at "accountability." Hegseth suggested the cuts targeted officers who failed to get on board with his efforts to ensure the military is focused on war-fighting rather than the "woke" policies of previous administrations, describing the reductions as an "accomplishment." FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Attacker's motive remain unknown after FlyDubai flight to Israel escapes disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79c92556a084b2b85d7beac65a75fb4ab343a0d254a36883a307637f29c043ff</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:40:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-attacker-s-motive-remain-unknown-after-flydubai-flight-to-israel-escapes-disaster" /><summary type="html">The motive of the Omani copilot who stabbed his captain on a flight to Israel, causing the plane to plummet dangerously and forcing it to land in Saudi Arabia, remained unknown on Thursday as investigators across the region raced to learn more. Israeli passengers who were on the FlyDubai aircraft carrying 174 people from the United Arab Emirates to Tel Aviv have described how the bloodied Indian captain managed to open the cockpit door to let them in before they grappled with the copilot and stabilised a descent so sharp that the plane’s rudder was torn away.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flydubai flight: How airlines prepare for emergencies?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caf94bfbd1f932589718bb399c364000e285473e10e098e80094fca0d1e8af92</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:39:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-flydubai-flight-how-airlines-prepare-for-emergencies" /><summary type="html">In the wake of the crash averted by passengers aboard a Flydubai flight to Israel on Wednesday, many questions have been raised about safety on the aircraft. How was the alert raised while the aircraft was rapidly losing altitude? How were passengers able to intervene in an area that is normally locked? Our colleagues at France 2 take a closer look at the facts and the unanswered questions, as well as current safety procedures.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM presents belt-tightening 2027 budget, including frozen wages and new taxes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d060560f479d995b31e01c5f5a360d43ea279be90e2876e46c865c7589d7ea8</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:20:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261001-french-pm-to-present-belt-tightening-2027-budget-including-frozen-wages-and-new-taxes" /><summary type="html">French Prime ​Minister ‌Sébastien Lecornu ⁠on Thursday presented a belt-tightening government budget for 2027, with savings predicted to come from freezing wages in the public sector and all but the lowest ‌pensions. A series of targeted tax measures were also predicted, though the country's independent fiscal watchdog said the plans to reduce the deficit were "limited" in light of the challenge facing the government.</summary><category term="France" /></entry></feed>
